qwen3_composition_verification_owner_clean_cut_anchor: "Use sole owner `tinyrustlm.qwen3-composition-verification-owner/1`: source 81,019 bytes/SHA256 `3a3894bf7a9a59b08b72e71a6d87e6f817c6e51fa1b67b2f6a60a9d70fe01c85`, profile 4,388 bytes/SHA256 `5f7a9a25350041069f1ba6cf417f4ed0f75c6d1d96ddbbdabae3b11718247cf8`, and architecture 12,827 bytes/SHA256 `32c44f7b0b86d46dce3ec7e6beed63b0e6210f29b34860c64d34b45fae2f0e43`. It alone owns converter and managed-inspector launch, create-only bounded raw streams, process terminals, exact ten-member graph validation, final verification v6, and later read-only verification. The superseded controller and dedicated test are absent from maintained source. Focused owner/profile/cutover is 22/22; with immutable `/9` registration/result it is 44/44; complete standard is 1,446/0/2 of 1,448. Exact clean implementation `a6a9a3354c1ef4fd34150829fe41e91fa3dbcf7f` is four-way remote exact; release run `c60ce2c5de0c77f9174ab8595cb33c0d209fb28051654a604046edb4a0ff38ac` passes ten shards and 23/23 with independently reproduced 3,995-byte aggregate SHA256 `e0b241870bf1ed760711a1aaeff5cf6a2c791f069eaa5e0feb0f0b40afc044b1` and empty stderr. The new twelve-agent packet is `docs/research-prompts/2026-08-25-twelve-disconnected-first-production-slm2-completion-research-prompts.md`, 80,891 ASCII/LF bytes, 1,365 lines, 10,086 words, SHA256 `f8e4035a3de802013d76232933b73acb9e97a80fa286e1046fc43c1177eb9831`; reports remain advisory. Commit/push/fresh-verify this evidence checkpoint, then preregister output-free `/10` against the exact implementation with wholly new absent names. This mechanism does not repair `/9` or prove a model, browser, quality, P2P, deployment, MemoryEndpoints, or campaign claim; counters remain zero."
qwen3_execution_v9_terminal_ambiguous_anchor: "Preserve canonical public result `contracts/vnext/qwen3-real-composition-execution-result.v9.json`, 16,578 bytes/SHA256 `e22ec93b089beb814ee88ba4221213e5eb73920f81fd74f5ce5eec547eab9414`, private verification 42,323 bytes/SHA256 `55bc8d97dc4f7e11cc6ec83723f2724e6bfe8654bf0b0ab61af7b92593ce3471`, and private 598,308,416-byte candidate SLM2 SHA256 `a0e351cdba8a4567d703e0f77c73c77ed08f783bb5420a19dfeef733c97cb2e7` as immutable `/9` history. Environment authority, Rust custody `/4`, managed custody `/4`, and the sole converter launch passed. Structural qualification did not pass because registered outer controller streams are absent and the one managed inspection rejected a noncanonical Windows path argument with `managed-inspection-intent-path`. The candidate is preserved but not qualified, adopted, releasable, publishable, or campaign-countable. Result commit `8f122de6659c9ec25efb9212ff7824250b6ed951` is pushed/four-way exact; standard is 1,436/0/2 of 1,438 and clean release run `1460e679b4d6ceae9c413d3d7c586d1d5ee487f6f5a27b9817513ebbd7117174` is 23/23 with verified 3,995-byte aggregate SHA256 `dc332237d459af514f89927324fd52a7204c0e2333f838c316ddd385dd96c44a`. Implement one source-owned end-to-end managed inspection/verification owner with canonical child arguments, create-only stream ownership, bounded process custody, independent rehash, and create-only final verification; fully test and clean-gate it before a separate output-free `/10` registration using wholly new absent names. MemoryEndpoints remains unauthorized/disconnected and all counters remain zero."
owned_application_data_build_custody_v4_anchor: "Use sole maintained technical custody profile `tinyrustlm.source-controlled-build-custody/4`, 10,274 bytes/SHA256 `26b75c36911c14d744a764c19d8a40ec0c28762add5e6616501080120aad9b45`, owner 103,310 bytes/SHA256 `4d0a86fccc7c798866a0c36538adb78bf73cb383f9d74e03d8794edf264040df`, and architecture 9,396 bytes/SHA256 `4e6c86c1a869b4c61f923e9c040018a333d80444f5ef95b3139400dadcd215de`. `/4` cleanly replaces `/3` and binds exact owned APPDATA, LOCALAPPDATA, TEMP, and TMP with five precreated/directly inspected directories. Generic installed-SDK TDD outside every registered operation proves no APPDATA causes the exact NETSDK1060/null-path1 class, APPDATA alone succeeds but leaves relative NuGet migration state, and APPDATA plus LOCALAPPDATA succeeds with all outputs and owned-local migration state. Implementation `7eb4c02fde4fd7710a0abff41703566f60221664`, tree `1f990bdbdbabba341a38310c55b5c3d52f5f24fa`, is pushed and four-way remote exact. Focused owner 21/21, SDK regression 1/1, combined immutable-closure 52/52, complete unit 1,414/0/2 of 1,416, and clean release 23/23 pass. Release run `dfea6f0678854e65e685edccc5fbaa4c809486478501345e3ae3521296e8731e` independently verifies to 3,995 bytes/SHA256 `6ff46548da9b46c6725d4e1216a1b8e503859fc7edf3f66d7d7364b9f40e4fd0`. The twelve-agent research packet is `docs/research-prompts/2026-08-25-twelve-disconnected-owned-appdata-qwen3-slm2-clean-cut-research-prompts.md`, 99,193 ASCII/LF bytes/SHA256 `f9ebd5a347277305b77a1299625249d3cbd10158f65ba148cc99377b11ad4f6e`; returned reports remain advisory. Commit/push/fresh-readback this evidence-only UAI checkpoint before separately preregistering output-free `/9` with new absent names. No `/9` material, model, browser, deployment, MemoryEndpoints, or counter evidence exists."
latest_human_prelaunch_single_product_rule_2026_08_25: "TinyRustLM remains one unreleased, unversioned product until the human explicitly changes this rule. There is no released V1 and therefore no product V2, legacy customer population, backward-compatibility duty, migration era, or accepted debt. Product UI, marketing, current documentation, architecture, and release plans must never frame the work as V2, vNext, next generation, old versus new, or a compatibility edition. Numbered technical identities such as SLM2, ACG2, Tokenizer2, Template2, Sampling2, Prompt2, schema revisions, receipt revisions, execution numbers, semantic package versions, and the current source-control branch identify exact bytes or evidence only. Keep one enterprise-quality owner and executable path for each responsibility. When a design is superseded, replace every maintained producer and consumer coherently, prove the complete replacement, and delete the superseded implementation, reader, writer, route, adapter, alias, flag, fixture, test assumption, current documentation claim, marketing claim, package input, and deployable byte in the same green change. Preserve immutable receipts and raw failures only as inert audit history. A known defect, duplicated path, temporary patch, weakened test, stale documentation, TODO deferral, or unreachable-but-maintained predecessor blocks release and deployment; rewrite freely when that yields the strongest architecture."
qwen3_execution_v8_terminal_managed_build_failure_anchor: "Preserve output-free registration `2a0e175daee7bd2810eab74f5daeeb0c7eda0aa3`, tree `37fc4adb26bc8c40229a81a038dcc1b9021014f0`, profile 61,969 bytes/SHA256 `4a7e255c500ef87e3ddac4d7befb7331232167e7bcf47aae6cdabfbd752fec21`, and canonical terminal result 16,999 bytes/SHA256 `9caa23225dfa2b0e01f4bfd550c0a4cf178d4d7db2f301159f0e2b040dd94f40`. Exact environment materialization and Rust custody `/3` passed once; Rust qualified the 240,128-byte x64 scratch inspector SHA256 `b038227799d03f322eb1b7ce55abe662b5ed1d481e37e282b186ecd545315c5c` and 852,992-byte x64 converter SHA256 `c90d963752f92c7de10866d071a9086334d5b80160de8815a508df2ff0a8d48c`. Managed custody ran once and terminally failed at child exit one with bounded `NETSDK1060` assets-lock read failure; no output or scratch inspection qualified and root cause remains false. Preserve all 12 created names; three composition names remain absent. The zero-byte `NuGet/Migrations/1` side effect SHA256 `e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855` is privately quarantined and must never enter Git. Commit/push/fresh-verify this closure; then use general isolated TDD to establish and remove the sole causal managed-build defect before a clean-gated output-free `/9` registration with new names. `/8` grants no managed qualification, conversion, SLM2, parity, browser, quality, P2P, publication, deployment, MemoryEndpoints, or counter credit."
