qwen3_execution_v4_build_custody_anchor: "Preserve output-free registration `8948baf1d21a73cde5781cf74a7c5020fd0b8cca`, tree `6a25e28f45b9bf69d82782efb965a9c0da5dee76`, profile SHA256 `f3f549a108c4a3acb767b241f2d1ef6d2db737c67442f059e8e943dabb992275`, and terminal public result `qwen3-real-composition-execution-result.v4.json`, 5,293 bytes/SHA256 `c928b55cf9eb871c09b7f1e1aacf1983bf3a7e2fe6ca4697aa58c50648187a35`. One Rust build was launched, but observer metadata failed before durable child-exit capture; exit status is unknown. Cargo `Finished` and candidate PE SHA256 `cd24a738b327b89d03501205301e89321bbd3955be91dfb245d2219a8b9201d5` are indirect only. Preserve existing control/build roots; later three roots never existed. Before `/5`, use one tested source-controlled custody owner that records exit status before optional diagnostics, then register wholly new roots output-free. No broader claim, MemoryEndpoints authority, or counter credit."
build_custody_terminal_status_authority: "A child build is successful only from the owned process API's durably captured exit status plus complete custody evidence. Capture and persist the exit status immediately after wait and before `ExitTime`, timestamps, executable inventory, PE inspection, or any optional diagnostic. Optional metadata failure must never erase status. Every spawn, timeout, overflow, nonzero, zero, and observer failure gets one create-only terminal record; post-exit files are observations, not substitutes for status."
prelaunch_single_product_authority: "TinyRustLM is one unversioned, unreleased product. There is no product V1 or V2, legacy product, compatibility edition, migration lane, fallback implementation, or accepted code debt. Technical identities such as SLM2, ACG2, Tokenizer2, Template2, Sampling2, Prompt2, vNext contract families, semantic versions, branch names, execution attempts, and UAI profile revisions are exact internal format/evidence identities only; they never create a second product generation or authorize duplicate product paths. Build the sole best current architecture directly. In the same fully tested replacement, repoint every maintained caller and delete every superseded executable reader, writer, route, schema, adapter, flag, test helper, maintained document, marketing claim, and packaged byte. Merely excluding old source from a build is not cleanup when a maintained command, script, package, or document can still reach it. Immutable historical evidence may remain only as inert, non-executable history. A release or deployment is ineligible while the registered obsolete closure, a stale product claim, a known defect, a temporary patch, a TODO deferral, or a weakened test remains."
qwen_tokenizer2_output_path_clean_cut_implementation_anchor: "Over remote-exact parent `c5f60e958872e125f52c9a5355eb7fdd4977b367`, current executable conversion owners use only Tokenizer2 `/2` SHA256 `97b381c73e7191f245ba132421a81bf015092b8550599413a6c81c6dae0afae4`, composition `/4` SHA256 `19e43c7ae532e7bc1822cbdcf179ee9bf1ed111298d3c6e5b13d37d990ee47e8`, exact `.tokenizer2`, member `tokenizer.tokenizer2`, and receipt v2. `.tok2` and all inexact paths reject with no output; `minimodel.tok2` remains only the binary format ID. Rust 34/34 plus full workspace and warnings-denied Clippy, Node 167/167, managed build 0/0 and tests 207/207 pass. Architecture is 6,281 bytes/SHA256 `14addb0b2e9508dce508455780bd067886d4a7fcfd5a1ebbcc7fad95a1fddf39`. Commit/push/fresh-verify before a new output-free one-shot registration. Preserve `/3`; no broader claim, MemoryEndpoints authority, or counter credit."
qwen3_execution_v3_tokenizer_path_clean_cut_anchor: "Preserve execution `/3` registration commit `43a29e8e1ba7a3296be18425a5fc077fb13617fe`, one-build/one-launch terminal result `qwen3-real-composition-execution-result.v3.json` at 8,773 bytes and SHA256 `2ae10fc8a76cced2e88d9b9c310af4eeb3ef436829f3f6a5ee8c551dfde6b2e4`, private verification SHA256 `88df285e0f64caac6c468512936ba1e269521287d85a95fbea8e79335c80eb48`, and partial 598,308,416-byte SLM2 SHA256 `a0e351cdba8a4567d703e0f77c73c77ed08f783bb5420a19dfeef733c97cb2e7`. `/3` rejected with `qwen-tokenizer2-output-path-invalid`; managed inspection did not run. Use output-free Tokenizer2 `/2` at 8,394 bytes/SHA256 `97b381c73e7191f245ba132421a81bf015092b8550599413a6c81c6dae0afae4` and composition `/4` at 11,421 bytes/SHA256 `19e43c7ae532e7bc1822cbdcf179ee9bf1ed111298d3c6e5b13d37d990ee47e8` to implement sole `.tokenizer2`, receipt v2, and zero executable predecessor support only after this checkpoint is pushed/fresh-exact. Internal `minimodel.tok2` remains a format ID, not a suffix. No broader claim; MemoryEndpoints unauthorized; counters zero."
release_surface_restart_activation_clean_gate_anchor: "Preserve implementation `ed6b2bfa4710a5c2a27716c6fe54803e7c8ea55b`, prior timeout run `b8851fe74916282f3fb9d74530788e5153b87b0c1f05375f93a109908082ef28`, and clean source `45ddff17cbfa14ff5343abbbdeb31dd846df805b`. Complete standard Node passes 1260/0/1 across 1261. Clean run `2325cab78fb411bea1cb1913e96e8a4018487eb702c790b29f73d696a1cf8f69` passes ten shards and 23/23 tests; independent verification reproduces 3995-byte aggregate SHA256 `7d1f71b72d4bb8bfa2c731ac3a7ba99405d7896aedc56ea84de0e28677ce6c2e`. Next preregister Qwen execution `/3` output-free with all-new roots, push/fresh-fetch it, build once, and execute once. This grants no broader claim or campaign credit."
qwen3_tied_output_correction_registration_anchor: "Use remote-exact source state `17d96a07d05a6735adc834112d5f7eb60b37914a`; source profile `/2` at 18,177 bytes and SHA256 `fa2ce18f38129a6b106000d7802d1ea3995921e2b945ae5e52457908f548e7cf`; composition profile `/3` at 9,764 bytes and SHA256 `c30dcc162cb563f91bc3571fa165f910670f819c5134eed3ecf16a1d38ba85c0`; and architecture SHA256 `dab7c1ff1c686700f4c3b18c80e8cc91054bf0e310f3b4438a24377f47f66dc1`. Implement only these identities: exactly 311 physical source tensors, 310 logical tensors, streamed exact tied-output equality before output creation, v2 receipt with separate physical/logical evidence, no duplicate emission, and full mismatch regressions. Clean-cut old executable IDs with no selector/reader/migration/alias/fallback. Registration created no output or broader claim; `/2` roots remain immutable, MemoryEndpoints unauthorized, counters zero."
qwen3_real_execution_v2_tied_output_defect_anchor: "Use remote-exact result commit `7314338e1f078f41fff690f74bccf0c9beca0c07`, result `qwen3-real-composition-execution-result.v2.json` at 8,275 bytes and SHA256 `4b2c957943d91fe7023d5ab78d2582735d21196e93403c212a9b104204bc970c`, and private verification SHA256 `95cb01c7f989f25db62fae8719e4389fc75d00b26dcf6c80ca4a17ccb116ed20`. `/2` ran both builds and one converter launch, then strictly rejected with `qwen3-tensor-inventory-mismatch`; managed inspection did not run. The exact locked source has 311 tensors: canonical 310 plus byte-identical tied `lm_head.weight` and `model.embed_tokens.weight`, each BF16 `[151936,1024]`, 311,164,928 bytes, SHA256 `8f29acf519434862d95613b2b4f6b9d14933a5e4d16baebf8ac0b33b410acfb6`. Correct the source profile generally: require exact redundant tied-output equality, retain 310 logical output tensors, reject every mismatch, then clean-cut the old producer/composition identities and use all-new execution roots. Preserve `/2` forever; no retry, managed laundering, cleanup, repair, compatibility, fallback, alias, migration, broader claim, MemoryEndpoints authority, or campaign credit."
qwen3_real_execution_v1_result_and_controller_anchor: "Use remote-exact inspector commit `b3f98d15262a23d2c876f16dec6414aec6b9ebb9`, result `qwen3-real-composition-execution-result.v1.json` at 4,076 bytes and SHA256 `dd1d9c85b5bb8bf098641a156de06e59243d88530434d70c574dcdceedb7a1ce`, controller `qwen3-composition-execution-controller.js` at 33,731 bytes and SHA256 `c78b6f8d59f61299aab511365fe8a699f6cd0a7989f222b954229d1d7e0e3508`, and inspect-only managed owner SHA256 `ed81944fd92fdb52ccc980af0969cda79393564b6217e8d8de0b23d84b16f031`. Registration `/1` completed one successful offline release build but stopped before private binding; no converter launch or output exists. Preserve its private evidence exactly and never resume, retry, clean, overwrite, repair, or relabel it. Register `/2` against wholly new control/build/evidence/managed-build/output roots. Require all expensive checks before evidence-root creation, exact controller plus Node executable/version/platform/architecture identity, binding as first member, one start authorization and owned process, separate bounded raw streams, post-exit executable/output hashes, one read-only managed inspection with no converter process API, no compatibility/debt/fallback, zero MemoryEndpoints authority, and zero campaign counters."
real_qwen3_execution_parity_browser_chat_research_anchor: "Use remote-exact research commit `a0b8cb61606fa8868612859352a3aa53e4fd1675` and `docs/research-prompts/2026-08-25-twelve-disconnected-real-qwen3-execution-parity-browser-chat-research-prompts.md`, 1,822 lines, 13,878 words, 111,822 bytes, SHA256 `7ac79d096d1486a3536ebcd0d5fbb3d9540fac2129668e543109cc751504ccb5`, as twelve completely standalone public-research assignments. They cover one-shot conversion custody, immutable Qwen3 tensor schema, mixed-Q8, six-artifact verification, source-framework first divergence, native Rust, browser WASM, KV/TurboQuant/TurboVec/Colibri/specialists, P2P-or-convert UX, untouched browser chat, no-cheat quality, and end-to-end release/docs. Reports are advisory inputs only and never private-code, conversion, runtime, browser, quality, P2P, publication, MemoryEndpoints, or campaign evidence. Intake them through the normal evidence-separated review process."
qwen3_real_source_and_composition_relationship_anchor: "Use public base source lock `qwen3-0.6b-base-source-lock.v1.json`, 1,901 bytes at SHA256 `e24bf9d95a5631e0b7c44c192e4ec6b7ec4b8793e1597f9dad99f1257ecf582d`, and sole executable complete-composition profile `tinyrustlm.qwen3-complete-composition-conversion/2`, 8,835 bytes at SHA256 `d6124b6acd174dc6188ca5d7b5a2d334fb33d00f7ef0364b56d9921051121718`. Source-lock commit `13a90b4dc07db2fc4c27b53f00ad9b9e69be8fae`, output-free registration `a7de8ececa877ab50c30e980fcf554c660068435`, and implementation `255f2641269ca08e1d169713091c12b075e061f9` are fresh-remote exact. Require equal model ID/revision, exact distinct model/tokenizer architecture profiles, and five shared byte-identical file records. Profile `/1` is terminally invalidated before real output and has no reader, migration, alias, fallback, or runtime support. Rust 29/29, managed Release 85/85, affected Node 123/123, focused correction 23/23, and warnings-denied Clippy pass. Register one zero-retry execution before any real conversion output. Structural conversion will not prove runtime, browser, quality, P2P, publication, or campaign progress; counters remain zero and MemoryEndpoints is unauthorized/disconnected."
tinyrustlm_web_release_0_3_0_anchor: "TinyRustLM.com release `0.3.0`, release date `2026-08-24`, was published from clean source commit `dca8a3a2107d8f6992291a59ae3eb1f319b332f4` at `2026-08-25T04:57:20.279Z`; publication ID is `cc53b43f55557aa9808264776c73168a750600c7b53c4d6a6bc61815afa0e3b2`. The canonical gate passed 1,202 with zero failures and one explicit absent-package-input skip across 1,203 standard tests, then 23/23 across ten serial release shards; run ID `d0f4fedab50db55b427a514f3242dab4bb0fabb80e524d8b397dc0d474bf2ce4`, aggregate SHA256 `b0fa4b267bdb8a406e4ccb4525e82e6c6423b4bd186c75ae64f8460890f1eb78`, and full-log SHA256 `677f504b9783ff6d76b2d623c0db2a4a6700b4909a8a4a5488f63bc6347f292c`. Immutable deployment report SHA256 `a50f142f9c121233e9548a34a3917554409be998d3ce8c8746418738a4e52005` proves 23/23 HTTPS readbacks, five retired model routes absent, zero secret findings, and zero hosted model bytes. Finalized ledger SHA256 `c1788f1f244e38f068b3df7639ba56eff8f30186c1167e9dee8f7f81e4de5955` is remote-exact at commit `5058012d2fbdfcf16edb75677d85e462b3962945`. This is web publication proof only. Companion packages, real Qwen3 SLM2 conversion, model quality, P2P outside proof, MemoryEndpoints, and campaign counters remain unproven; counters stay 0/20, 0/50, 0/25, 0/40, 0/20."
release_failure_root_closure_anchor: "Use remote-exact correction commit `0343da897c335ca6177606b7563dd8a6e4fcb151`, tree `3be0c1b50c5092e879cd74a6643e05cd70e79f74`, descended from registered implementation `e214c51c21d1bc5bf9e5016cfbab01ec8983786c`, as the current deterministic release-root closure. Preserve pre-registration feature build `db7cc1c03b09b89a5fff7f127f0bd437c0d33d17` as rejected history. Preserve the first full run from clean `93b2a28777c2ee158085416b2f4caa1d19544ff8`: 1,203 tests, 1,201 pass, one fail, one skip; its 212,678-byte log SHA256 is `966de5334b947c7461081e225894bb102b0cfca10c74268fd82741a4db180903`. That run exposed one stale acquisition-test assertion and was not rewritten. The narrow correction binds exact truthful `Public package pending` and `Deployment blocked` statuses and passes 5/5. The canonical complete gate from clean remote-exact `0343da8` passes its standard partition with 1,203 tests, 1,202 pass, zero fail, and one explicit package-input skip; release-surface run `f4006a6662ae617bfffb990c7ea28ce125a3e41944505def76b811ea0c2d0b25` passes 23/23 across 10 serial shards with 3,995-byte aggregate SHA256 `8b9894164b115eeb3ca2c10fc6faf108f2605a1aecde72b961f0b919a958c28d`. The complete 203,658-byte log SHA256 is `8620e877365c545b0a5f7d0f618196b37e6ad72efa189aa5ba0754fb0c80db98`. The skip requires four generated NuGet package inputs under the external package lane and grants no package evidence. Source/release-surface roots are green; package publication, web deployment/readback, real model, quality, P2P, MemoryEndpoints, and campaign progress remain separate gates."
tokenizer2_browser_gate_descendant_revalidation_anchor: "Preserve completed Tokenizer2 browser-WASM registration `/1` and never rerun it. Descendant audit at source `84fe6c2078851dbfef95f0fde64f22d17ef39a12` produced no comparative output: focused current-source tests pass 35/35 with 5,856-byte external log SHA256 `32e57baaa16e0bd97d898e85dbf7cdcef664725e09713856fdf4aaabb21eefe9`; direct artifact inspection reconfirms 7,038,773 bytes at `cbbf907ed95150c4db920c36cee9ab13eca2a3c6d2dcffb6bf5d7ac5b95b8f7b`, TOK2/technical 2.0, 151,669 total, 151,643 base, 26 added, 151,387 merges, and zero reserved header bytes. Private output remains exactly run hashes `0ed18293784438035b06d99e8709c382ccef1a775c70f00d624a3964d3c92905`, `fb493d2e251c8efa6e12d73664aa319ad4901235fa46edf5b00fc4b43806e920`, and result `f828190b2ff5d3c1e794cb50f3b0dd8c41367ed09fca758eeb513fb1ec2c964e`; external and committed result bytes match, and the profile parent is empty/non-reparse. No material identity drift exists. Consume this immutable dependency and continue the first real SLM2 vertical slice plus release-failure closure; do not preregister or execute a duplicate Tokenizer2 experiment."
companion_loopback_listener_host_anchor: "Use sole profile `tinyrustlm.companion.loopback-capability/3` at 11,836 bytes and SHA256 `a4f8574a6d35f8c66f537f8e4e2c7d659a239a6267d60c26210672db72929d28`, remote-exact implementation commit `e544a3a2c6632282a005efae2fa566e8afd2717a`, tree `c2e3a259884ce48ab1ea1951a078d6b2a3d01488`, listener SHA256 `648b559a8179992e736a0ea51f123d96bf72bf56c194057fb035b37c7013d111`, host SHA256 `76be51d11fcccb204fb4ef02836a999ec0ea26b88be2f8535143bbfedb411bb2`, and ADR SHA256 `9f4b9a661c3113b3a639f169587e4d17b5b4d83c80eab0c8ac72e8b287e21612` as the sole current Companion listener/host authority. Preserve numeric IPv4 `127.0.0.1`, OS port zero, HTTP/1.1, closed Host/Origin/CORS/framing/header/body/timeout/connection limits, parser-owned malformed framing, application-owned canonical bounded errors, one post-bind interactive TRLC1 line, and unavailable operation routes. Managed solution 203/203, focused listener/error 14/14, and registration `/1`/`/2`/`/3` 39/39 pass. Preserve all three recorded failure observations. Complete Node remains 1,182 pass, 15 fail, one skip in 1,198 and blocks deployment. Next implement one memory-only physical-browser client and finish the production Tokenizer2 WASM gate. This is not browser, transfer, model, quality, release, deployment, MemoryEndpoints, or campaign proof; counters remain zero."
tokenizer_browser_release_failure_research_anchor: "Use remote-exact research commit `3beeae8c631304bbc63f421dba2ffe0c02c61765`, tree `d1de170aa636f8fcab19002cab09c4452b86db69`, and `docs/research-prompts/2026-08-24-twelve-disconnected-tokenizer-browser-release-failure-resolution-research-prompts.md` at 1,450 lines, 11,499 words, SHA256 `f76d1aa87786fb60a65dd3d2ab7b479f87bbafdf97c2429fc6bdce61ad0753ac` as twelve source-independent research assignments. They cover Cargo custody, registration DAGs, exact Qwen3 Tokenizer2, raw WASM, Worker cancellation, differential parity, Template2/Prompt2, HTTPS-to-loopback policy, two-profile Chromium, deterministic app assets, release scanning, and root-cause closure. Reports are advisory input only, never private-code, test, browser, model, release, or deployment evidence."
companion_rotation_revocation_anchor: "Use remote-exact commit `6537c6070ecd109c65791493864d8bd90ac8971d`, tree `fc988afd8d9c21d13ca6a90b6abe7194e13afc6e`, architecture SHA256 `821cfc368088d1ad8eb7f8410e0d40b9469dd2b00f289567bf10662623327542`, and corrected profile `/2` as the sole status/rotation/revocation state authority. Preserve one exact 120-second pending rotation, old-key request authentication plus candidate-new-key proof, epoch ceiling 64, sequence/key-age reset with unchanged absolute expiry, 30-second exact old-commit replay only, replay rate bound, response-before-erasure revocation, process-lifetime revoked tombstones, fail-closed 4,096-record admission, and open/executing/finished lease cleanup. Managed 189/189 and browser/oracle 8/8 pass. Next implement strict numeric-loopback Kestrel and raw-socket rejection, then one memory-only browser client. This is not listener, browser, transfer, model, release, deployment, MemoryEndpoints, or campaign proof; current complete Node 15 failures block deployment and counters remain zero."
companion_installation_pairing_session_anchor: "Use remote-exact commit `66248fd95443b5cdeac5936502a33d4488fcc235`, tree `a7ea0d31a2d0901f58994463f58825e717d7fa90`, architecture SHA256 `2669c904cfdaf457815e806c4368e3fda07c42d3dcd6242f401cc2059b224fe2`, and corrected profile `/2` as the sole installation/pairing/session state authority. Preserve create-only canonical installation bytes, private platform permissions, nondurable process identity, explicit single-use TRLC1, monotonic 30/60/300-second rules, bounded first-winner pairing, four memory-only sessions, exact proof/sequence commit, one in flight, rolling limits, expiry, proven response bytes, and key clearing. Managed 180/180 and browser/oracle 8/8 pass; Linux still needs real execution. Next implement exact rotation and revocation before any listener. This is not listener, browser, transfer, model, release, deployment, MemoryEndpoints, or campaign proof; full Node 15 failures block deployment."
companion_loopback_codec_vectors_anchor: "Use remote-exact implementation `9eb7163ea4659d088b66a5143243c708dfe14bb3`, tree `e226939116c0fbfb93c6cc341c4e9b1d2a564377`, under sole corrected profile `/2`. Preserve 4,731-byte nonsecret vector corpus SHA256 `6fb87e2ccebaf3c15c7af3452e05ee35c44ece40b8abf3ed1e45b9985cfc0e15` and architecture SHA256 `db52ab23b74fa5815ab945ab2180b61152b33580d328362f09a68b411273ec82`. Native and browser implementations must retain exact u32 UTF-8 framing, proof/HKDF field order, operation-specific verification, metadata binding, canonical installation bytes, and equal hostile validation. Independent Node crypto recomputes every vector; browser 8/8 and managed 169/169 pass. Browser WebCrypto remains outside deployable app bytes until the complete client cutover; then move it to registered app ownership and delete the tool path and old bridge, retaining no duplicate owner. Next implement durable installation and fake-time pairing/session state. Unit vectors are not listener, physical browser, model, release, deployment, MemoryEndpoints, or campaign evidence; full Node 15 failures still block deployment."
companion_loopback_capability_registration_anchor: "Use remote-exact corrected output-free commit `912f8ebe1a2b774977eaf2ed298d8ac162d35fa0`, tree `f89b28db05b340e82b0aac96d9856c0b8b15252e`, profile `tinyrustlm.companion.loopback-capability/2` at 22,681 bytes and SHA256 `6ad07dda97ae50d8e6c3fc1a581e6742d2e18c66484a4a9864e1b3bc7a57ae81`, and correction record at 13,411 bytes and SHA256 `b574af05032bd52f7b37ffc831e1661eb9625e88afcf629f7e24ffc648be28f4` as the sole Companion browser-transport implementation authority. Profile `/1` at SHA256 `81e3f2f3795a51c0bce86e1aca66f6a7234608a3dd044cd7a9b1cbbf90c9ba77` is immutable non-executable history because its pairing/HKDF/rotation field order and several wire rules were incomplete; no output occurred. Implement exact canonical JSON, u32-framed transcripts, proof and HKDF fields, response-metadata binding, sequence commit, error/status, projection, and preflight rules from `/2`, plus the adopted exact `/1` numeric-loopback/route/limit/transfer boundary. Delete the old fixed-port health/bearer/BroadcastChannel bridge with no adapter. Corrected focused tests pass 56/56. The complete Node gate remains 1,150 pass, 15 fail, one skip; deployment stays blocked until every root cause is fixed."
managed_complete_composition_integration_anchor: "Use output-free reconciliation registration `af7857bbc4afa122d8013f2952b2944b53b6e3d2`, machine SHA256 `087038104f63d6e78373691034aaf586de803059d68c47a12acc2140bf3ac971`, and remote-exact implementation `87a0fc1c799f5359b44e3e5bdcb35b2d3500f22c`, tree `5327e22727b7fc3ac7dbb8c67b7f92f2bbc418a2`, as the sole managed complete-composition and Companion source-conversion/reconciliation authority. Preserve canonical create-only `source-conversion.intent.json`, operation schema `tinyrustlm.companion.operation.v2`, intent-before-Converting hash binding, separated durable `tinyrustlm.verified-composition.v1` and live `tinyrustlm.composition-conversion-live-observation.v1`, and read-only terminal inspection. Pending reconciliation performs no write, launch, adoption, retry, kill, or inference; exact pass advances to Available, exact native rejection advances to Rejected, and malformed/colliding/identity-drifted terminal evidence rejects with a bounded stable code. Preserve operation-v1 rejection, terminal immutability, cancellation race rules, source/tool removal recovery, and prohibition on laundering known live violations through durable pass evidence. Managed 163/163 with zero skips and preregistration 12/12 pass. Next output-free preregister one exact numeric-loopback capability protocol before any listener output. This is not real-model, browser, quality, P2P, publication, deployment, MemoryEndpoints, or campaign evidence; counters remain zero."
