complete_qwen3_composition_transaction_anchor: "Use output-free registration `afc53619343a7d46acafa6558babe288c3bf342c`, profile SHA256 `2f95f79783ec6cd12160d51f9697c5c77aab2e6cd46afeb5140fdb513e5d8158`, and remote-exact implementation `b75a70d8a2ddb741a3a81827adbc30c9d999699c`, tree `43ad1d77f423aba6c2e615a4da5af71693e505eb`, as the sole complete conversion authority. `tinyrustlm-convert qwen3-composition` requires related exact model/tokenizer source locks, emits exact SLM2/Tokenizer2/Template2/Sampling2/Prompt2/ACG2 plus bounded create-only evidence, independently reparses every member, verifies fixed identities and SLM2-Prompt2 vocabulary/context, resolves one member at a time, preflights complete resources, and preserves truthful nonretryable terminal rejection. Component commands are private compiler primitives, not product success. Affected Rust 60/60, workspace locked check, warnings-denied Clippy, Node/Chromium 40/40, package/docs 38/38, and hygiene checks pass. No real complete source run or product claim exists. Next integrate this exact terminal boundary into private managed Conversion and Companion, then preregister secure explicit-consent browser transport."
private_companion_foundation_clean_cut_anchor: "Use implementation commit `560eba955e8eb22e1521eaae25d9de66843937a4`, tree `b9e9356f6c0d3fbc32bde44f55af22f1ce7dd464`, as the sole current private-companion and managed-package foundation. Public packages are exactly Abstractions, Core, and P2P; MemoryEndpoints is optional/unauthorized/disconnected, Conversion is private optional tooling, and Companion is private/nonpackable/package-reference-free. Preserve schemas `tinyrustlm.companion.acquire.v1` and `tinyrustlm.companion.operation.v1`, immutable source/profile identities, explicit source approval and byte ceiling, no more than two ordered HTTPS peers, deterministic operation identity, closed branches/states, terminal immutability, owned-root create-only bounded JSON journaling, and exact six-member composition completeness. The public SeedHost source/tool/tests and obsolete package/release/E2E/sibling-executable paths are deleted with no compatibility authority. Companion 10/10, package 38/38, Core 49/49, managed solution 97/97 with zero skips, browser acquisition 5/5, script syntax, diff hygiene, and frozen goal identity pass. Clean source `560eba9` produced a create-only external win-x64 package transaction with zero-defect audit `8f0c035ca04ef94ea72597523356f65a3881e64169f4518a84c66cd52bc4da0b` and hash manifest `dfc0bbd898e769f409035fd8281de39425a205be040ecf2dd2f1d438d0e000d0`. This is local foundation/package evidence only. Push and fresh-fetch the checkpoint, then implement one complete create-only six-artifact Rust conversion transaction before companion/browser transport."
qwen3_slm2_converter_implementation_anchor: "Use sole Qwen3 model-converter implementation commit `d0e2a099be75abe4353e808769fb896b9c483a3a`, tree `41178a07d627abf107c6e514ded2efc384dc08f0`, proven equal across local HEAD, tracking, fresh FETCH_HEAD, and actual remote. It implements preregistered profile `tinyrustlm.qwen3-safetensors-to-slm2-mixed-q8/1` at SHA256 `313069152daa70a2c2b5070f9d1350379a5800f647d5c3ac8d23a75ff9ead968` as the only model-conversion command, deletes the executable Qwen2/F32 converter and test corpus, and emits only one independently reparsed mixed-Q8 `.slm2` plus its create-only conversion receipt. Bind implementation record 7,267 bytes at `6dfdaa1da511752d1d575b970d8ce0332dfec405a0b437e37dcabe471c3b0e8d`, Rust owner 48,397 bytes at `e36b3b1cf133002cfd4ea63b77772e98979a9972ab8579a399472cf80dfe2640`, and 28,214-byte Qwen3 corpus at `645b5bcc7b36ccc71fe9973c9046293f07c8b128f0ac6c67a5ba2bee1f5d9aed`. Preserve strict nine-file source closure, exact Qwen3 GQA/head-dimension/QK-normalization semantics, bounded BF16/F32 streaming, direct role-owned Q8/F32 storage without dense shadow or runtime repacking, source rehash, independent complete SLM2 reparse, create-only promotion, public-safe errors, and separated quality/runtime claims. Warnings-denied Rust passes 22/22, contract tests 22/22, public-safety tests 19/19, rustfmt, Clippy, strict JSON, ASCII/NUL, diff, and secret scans. No real model, parity, inference, quality, browser chat, P2P, package, deployment, publication, MemoryEndpoints, or campaign claim follows; counters remain 0/20, 0/50, 0/25, 0/40, and 0/20. Continue with the canonical host/runtime consumer rewrite and deletion of every superseded SLM1/ACG1 executable path."
prompt2_q8_implementation_anchor: "Use sole Prompt2 implementation commit `fb321d4ce9eec0510162a27e4527bc626a307755`, tree `e7660a01762b137b6ebb173df267ae370b2797b2`, proven equal across local, tracking, FETCH_HEAD, and actual remote. Bind profile `f9eb4cbecfb52f5e2857216c999754da94021a5427a86732d33fe15efc0d062c`, canonical artifact `27aaed18b62930213a2395e398e68d18a90d4280e24c23d794e3e94352d7e1f3`, vectors `4b4a4497245ee371e4f3e2b930e3413caa0f8bb70b04c3385880b11de83c487e`, and independent Node source `7beb1edec00d0f24f8c308419a0b00e30abee090c331a5d563a6783f4e9f04ef`. Prompt2 now binds mixed-Q8 SLM2 format `5ac819cb31a17a64bec0d5492962a4baf0bd2778f6213b87c85c0a04f3a738d8` and runtime-Q8 vectors `c437ebb5e59c9059c49324d12d43e556493e62f5d6b2e857e369ca08674333a0`; exact superseded digests are hostile vectors. Preserve unchanged Tokenizer2, Template2, Sampling2, wires, composition semantics, limits, and standalone lock."
acg2_champion_format_implementation_anchor: "Use sole unpromoted ACG2 implementation commit `c489801d01d10e1445b42599efb58f83550479d1`, tree `4acade20b3704c2449038480bb35ba778924c90c`, proven exact across local, tracking, fresh FETCH_HEAD, and actual remote. It descends only from corrected output-free registration `416c3c1154b86feed5bdc41751609f4670462981`; preserve first registration `afec4dccad2062728677b6987519ce2385a1bca3761fe8f0927ac80242d6403d` as terminally-superseded-before-output audit history. Bind profile `944ed9b5b0ee2605ebb9ac13f2e5388c181bc857fdbfc082e62e9ae7b07c79be`, vectors `d7f0f956ccbc909b242d24410ff9f2f60216d8ff8537a108bff0f698c7b6a441`, Node oracle `301c32f645e11c25b93f7d9e5d44eaa882998e13bc3e526687d29a6ca533e916`, canonical graph `2f45314ae3617c348beff2617927d08dbe0058dd947d01b4f89aa77e0f57e9ff`, graph identity `b738c7ee4d67cd09bb3ae4f4eb8d31ab98a15e1d5d982f35cf6aac1a87ac394f`, and exact 896-byte five-member order. Preserve one-source/1-MiB streaming verification, canonical owner parsing, Prompt2 dependency closure, complete preflight, stale-operation rejection, one fail-atomic ownership swap, KV/generation invalidation, transcript preservation, unsafe-free Rust, and import-free Node/fresh-Chromium WASM conformance. This is technical fixture evidence for one prelaunch product, not a product V2, real model, quality, product browser chat, release, deployment, publication, P2P, MemoryEndpoints, or campaign pass."
slm2_q8_weight_profile_implementation_anchor: "Preserve exact remote-verified implementation commit `005be4efbcacd0301888df0b12d0db9f1611be58` and tree `5a561fd238f2552dd63b4d3f7e3a2a7e4fb346bd`. The sole production-bound model profile is mixed row-wise Q8 matrices/embeddings plus F32 normalization and optional biases with independent F32 KV. Bind format `5ac819cb31a17a64bec0d5492962a4baf0bd2778f6213b87c85c0a04f3a738d8`, weight profile `7e931fd23fa8f6a90c53e4c14c5630eef8ce87e0f0902acd5a5e2df03c60733a`, canonical artifact `4383b112797b99232561b67bdc752d8ea0e62e90e24f8b94fd629c563e2d1502`, runtime vectors `c437ebb5e59c9059c49324d12d43e556493e62f5d6b2e857e369ca08674333a0`, and hostile-corpus manifest `f3fa27a94b3e9b7e4004c041cec67adf31c9ab7f81a10daadbff8ffbabb65bc9`. Preserve direct artifact execution without F32 weight shadow or runtime repacking, exact 128-byte quant record, binary32 half-away-from-zero quantization, no-FMA scalar order, independent Node/Rust reproduction, every-prefix rejection, 20-seed typed replay, and identical Node/Chromium WASM vectors. This is fixture conformance only; continue the registered all-consumer replacement and delete superseded executable paths before promotion."
bounded_release_store_anchor: "Use receipt profile `1721e8d26cfd93617ce570a744796c8d95d5fc1fd628ac3ee94f1a484832ade5`, subject profile `63cd21ef8dda687f06c486c373840ed101fe2534d7b769d943064571416f94e5`, runner profile `c7e85b52c34fac59b65edee68d048c51fcdb5580321eb538dccc07c1164f68c3`, and release-surface profile `a7d82d79e28ee6fded64a47ad0be4a47003fe498a1de835824d2ff2b425f57ee` as the sole current generation-only contracts. Preserve one validated rebuild per open, generation-only same-process synchronization, stale-instance rebuild before access, immutable zero-scan same-open snapshots, exact physical authoritative observations, shared receipt-closure reads, bounded suffix batches, exact-prefix resume through 1,024, and final commit last. Clean commit `5c632d6cb101595c675e4c404be082087b8f2f13` passes release-surface run `4ec348ab4d790739add83c01ed5775e34626ddae0bb5c86c9b6cc2231fa82409`: 10/10 serial shards, 23/23 tests, 3,995-byte aggregate SHA256 `a2cca011202ebcf0b82b962aeccf012a84051189e95f8679c6f9a7f6463df91d`, independently reproduced. The complete generated-byte target passes in 165,509.3389 ms under the unchanged 180,000 ms ceiling. Make no broader product, deployment, or campaign claim."
