prelaunch_single_product_anchor: "Maintain one canonical enterprise-quality TinyRustLM prelaunch product architecture. No TinyRustLM product version has launched: there is no released V1 and therefore no product V2, old product generation, migration era, compatibility population, grandfathered behavior, or legacy customer contract. Never use V2, vNext, next generation, legacy, or compatibility language to frame the product, its UI, marketing, documentation, runtime, or release plan. Treat SLM2, Tokenizer2, Template2, Sampling2, Prompt2, ACG2, numbered schemas, package semantic versions, paths, and branch names only as exact technical identities for bytes, protocols, evidence, or source control. Choose the strongest coherent design, keep one owner and one executable truth path per responsibility, replace every affected dogfood producer and consumer together, verify the complete closure end to end, and delete every superseded executable path, adapter, alias, fixture, test assumption, documentation claim, and release input in the same completed major change. Retain old bytes only as immutable non-executable audit evidence. A build pass is the minimum checkpoint, not permission to retain known debt, temporary architecture, duplicated behavior, weakened tests, stale docs, low-quality patches, dead code, or deferred cleanup. Rewrite coherently whenever preserving an inferior path would create debt."
canonical_companion_anchor: "The sole current companion authority is the private nonpackable operation and reconciliation kernel at implementation commit `87a0fc1c799f5359b44e3e5bdcb35b2d3500f22c`. It uses `tinyrustlm.companion.operation.v2` and a canonical create-only source-conversion intent; operation.v1 is rejected and has no migration reader. It has no current listener, route, port, server, pairing, capability token, installer, service, browser bridge, or release identity. Preregister one closed secure browser-to-numeric-loopback capability protocol before implementation and physically verify it before use. Never restore or adapt the deleted SeedHost route family, old state/cross-tab identities, package surface, or instruction-file handoff."
canonical_companion_evidence_anchor: "Current Core tests pass 80/80, Companion tests pass 45/45, package tests pass 38/38, and the complete managed solution passes 163/163 with zero skips; reconciliation preregistration passes 12/12. Formatting, warnings-as-errors build, diff hygiene, exact 49-entry public API baseline, secret/private-path scans, and frozen-goal identity pass. Clean source `87a0fc1` produced a create-only external win-x64 package transaction with zero-defect audit SHA256 `b9c11d61c0957597331823024d6e309865ff70fb7ef92035e2fad61451bdf231` and hash-manifest SHA256 `228af1b0d0a6397e40e94d2df380328da819a7f89107719ce2991ba9b8d8e513`. This is local source/package evidence only, not Linux execution, signing, publication, deployment, public readback, server operation, real-model acquisition, or browser chat."
canonical_companion_next_anchor: "Output-free preregister the exact numeric-loopback capability contract before creating any listener, route, discovery document, pairing flow, or browser request. Then implement and fault-test that protocol, bounded six-artifact transfer, browser atomic storage and activation, Worker cancellation/recovery, and one provenance-bound real Qwen3 composition. Add no process relaunch/adoption inference, compatibility reader, migration, alias, fallback, retry selection, response repair, instruction download, fake success, or debt."
